Original commit body from 8a360c7fed08544974bacd365018cac61c5f38c0:

record_declaration (Java 16) was not an enclosing type to
_get_class_ancestors and had no symbol arm, so a file holding one record
emitted nothing. A record nested in a class had its methods named on the
OUTER class (Launcher.call for Launcher.RemoteLaunchCallable.call), so they
collected the outer class's callers and overrides.

- A record is a `record` symbol (registered kind, "Java 14+"), via one
  table-driven arm now shared with class and interface.
- Its components are emitted as private final fields, through one
  _java_field_symbol helper the field arm also uses.
- compact_constructor_declaration is a constructor; its signature is the
  record's components. The DDG walks it.
- The three class/interface/enum type-kind filters derive from one set, so
  records reach class_symbols (instantiation resolves: `new R(..)`).
- The containment linker treats `record` as a container.

A/B surveys against dev: records trino 836, kafka 258, spring-boot 137,
jenkins 10; instantiates +4,480 on trino. calls fall on trino (-2,942):
every lost edge was classified -- 3,624 went into misnamed record members,
164 were calls bound to an unrelated same-named class, the rest re-anchor
onto the record or resolve to a better target (2 unclassified).

